Feature: Agent Log Calculated Field Extraction and Validation

  The system must generate the calculated fields for the agent_log table in the purgo_playground schema of the purgo_databricks Unity Catalog, based on the mapping specification and source tables. The calculated fields must be derived using specific join logic, field selection, hardcoded values, and surrogate key generation. All validation, error handling, and business rules must be strictly enforced.

  Background:
    Given the following source tables exist in purgo_playground:
      | session_tracking_data      |
      | user_presence_tracker      |
      | agent_profile_data         |
    And the target table agent_log exists with the required columns
    And the mapping specification for agent_log is available
    And the hashing algorithm for agent_key is SHA256
    And the hardcoded location fields are always used (city: "New York", state: "NY", country: "USA", zip_code: "10001")
    And the most recent unix_id and full_name are determined by the latest last_modified_timestamp in agent_profile_data
    And missing or inconsistent data in joins must result in error logging to agent_log_error_log

  Scenario Outline: Successful calculated field extraction for agent_log (happy path)
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", session_start_time "<session_start_time>", session_end_time "<session_end_time>"
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", email_address "<email_address>"
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with email_address "<email_address>", internal_user_key "<internal_user_key>", full_name "<full_name>", last_modified_timestamp "<last_modified_timestamp>"
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log contains a record with:
      | unix_id                | "<internal_user_key>"         |
      | agent_name             | "<full_name>"                 |
      | log_date               | "<log_date>"                  |
      | agent_first_login      | "<first_login>"               |
      | agent_first_logout     | "<first_logout>"              |
      | total_login_time_hrs   | "<total_login_time_hrs>"      |
      | agent_city             | "New York"                    |
      | agent_state            | "NY"                          |
      | agent_country          | "USA"                         |
      | agent_zip_code         | "10001"                       |
      | data_loaded_at         | "<data_loaded_at>"            |
      | agent_key              | "<agent_key>"                 |
    And agent_log_error_log does not contain an error for this record

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | session_start_time     | session_end_time       | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   | log_date    | first_login           | first_logout          | total_login_time_hrs | data_loaded_at        | agent_key                                      |
      | A123              | 2025-01-01T08:00:00Z  | 2025-01-01T17:00:00Z   | agent1@company.com    | IU001            | John Doe       | 2025-01-01T18:00:00Z      | 2025-01-01  | 2025-01-01T08:00:00Z  | 2025-01-01T17:00:00Z  | 9.0                  | 2025-01-01T18:01:00Z  | <SHA256 of all fields>                         |
      | B456              | 2025-01-02T09:00:00Z  | 2025-01-02T18:30:00Z   | agent2@company.com    | IU002            | Jane Smith     | 2025-01-02T19:00:00Z      | 2025-01-02  | 2025-01-02T09:00:00Z  | 2025-01-02T18:30:00Z  | 9.5                  | 2025-01-02T19:01:00Z  | <SHA256 of all fields>                         |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - missing email_address in user_presence_tracker
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", session_start_time "<session_start_time>", session_end_time "<session_end_time>"
    And user_presence_tracker does not contain a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>"
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log_error_log contains a record with:
      | error_type    | "MissingEmailAddress" |
      | error_message | "No email_address found for person_identifier <person_identifier> in user_presence_tracker" |
      | error_time    | "<data_loaded_at>"    |
    And agent_log does not contain a record for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | session_start_time     | session_end_time       | data_loaded_at        |
      | C789              | 2025-01-03T08:00:00Z  | 2025-01-03T17:00:00Z   | 2025-01-03T18:01:00Z  |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - missing agent_profile_data for email_address
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", session_start_time "<session_start_time>", session_end_time "<session_end_time>"
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", email_address "<email_address>"
    And agent_profile_data does not contain a record with email_address "<email_address>"
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log_error_log contains a record with:
      | error_type    | "MissingAgentProfileData" |
      | error_message | "No agent_profile_data found for email_address <email_address>" |
      | error_time    | "<data_loaded_at>"        |
    And agent_log does not contain a record for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | session_start_time     | session_end_time       | email_address         | data_loaded_at        |
      | D012              | 2025-01-04T08:00:00Z  | 2025-01-04T17:00:00Z   | agent3@company.com    | 2025-01-04T18:01:00Z  |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - missing session_end_time in session_tracking_data
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", session_start_time "<session_start_time>", session_end_time NULL
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", email_address "<email_address>"
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with email_address "<email_address>", internal_user_key "<internal_user_key>", full_name "<full_name>", last_modified_timestamp "<last_modified_timestamp>"
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log_error_log contains a record with:
      | error_type    | "MissingSessionEndTime" |
      | error_message | "No session_end_time found for person_identifier <person_identifier>" |
      | error_time    | "<data_loaded_at>"      |
    And agent_log does not contain a record for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | session_start_time     | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp   | data_loaded_at        |
      | E345              | 2025-01-05T08:00:00Z  | agent4@company.com    | IU004            | Alice Brown    | 2025-01-05T18:00:00Z      | 2025-01-05T18:01:00Z  |

  Scenario Outline: Multiple agent_profile_data records for same email_address - select most recent
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", session_start_time "<session_start_time>", session_end_time "<session_end_time>"
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", email_address "<email_address>"
    And agent_profile_data contains multiple records with email_address "<email_address>", internal_user_key "<internal_user_key_1>", full_name "<full_name_1>", last_modified_timestamp "<last_modified_timestamp_1>"
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with email_address "<email_address>", internal_user_key "<internal_user_key_2>", full_name "<full_name_2>", last_modified_timestamp "<last_modified_timestamp_2>"
    And <last_modified_timestamp_2> is later than <last_modified_timestamp_1>
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log contains a record with:
      | unix_id      | "<internal_user_key_2>" |
      | agent_name   | "<full_name_2>"         |
      | log_date     | "<log_date>"            |
      | agent_first_login | "<first_login>"    |
      | agent_first_logout | "<first_logout>"  |
      | total_login_time_hrs | "<total_login_time_hrs>" |
      | agent_city   | "New York"              |
      | agent_state  | "NY"                    |
      | agent_country| "USA"                   |
      | agent_zip_code | "10001"               |
      | data_loaded_at | "<data_loaded_at>"    |
      | agent_key    | "<agent_key>"           |

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | session_start_time     | session_end_time       | email_address         | internal_user_key_1 | full_name_1   | last_modified_timestamp_1 | internal_user_key_2 | full_name_2   | last_modified_timestamp_2 | log_date    | first_login           | first_logout          | total_login_time_hrs | data_loaded_at        | agent_key                                      |
      | F678              | 2025-01-06T08:00:00Z  | 2025-01-06T17:00:00Z   | agent5@company.com    | IU005A             | Bob White     | 2025-01-06T17:00:00Z      | IU005B             | Robert White  | 2025-01-06T18:00:00Z      | 2025-01-06  | 2025-01-06T08:00:00Z  | 2025-01-06T17:00:00Z  | 9.0                  | 2025-01-06T18:01:00Z  | <SHA256 of all fields>                         |

  Scenario Outline: Surrogate key generation validation
    Given all required fields for agent_log are present for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log.agent_key is the SHA256 hash of the concatenated values of:
      | unix_id                |
      | agent_name             |
      | log_date               |
      | agent_first_login      |
      | agent_first_logout     |
      | total_login_time_hrs   |
      | agent_city             |
      | agent_state            |
      | agent_country          |
      | agent_zip_code         |
      | data_loaded_at         |

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | unix_id | agent_name | log_date    | agent_first_login     | agent_first_logout    | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at        | expected_agent_key                           |
      | G901              | IU006   | Carl Black | 2025-01-07  | 2025-01-07T08:00:00Z | 2025-01-07T17:00:00Z  | 9.0                  | New York   | NY         | USA          | 10001         | 2025-01-07T18:01:00Z  | <SHA256 of all fields>                       |

  Scenario Outline: Data type and format validation
    Given agent_log contains a record for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"
    Then agent_log.unix_id is a non-null string
    And agent_log.agent_name is a non-null string
    And agent_log.log_date is a valid date in "YYYY-MM-DD" format
    And agent_log.agent_first_login is a valid timestamp in "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ" format
    And agent_log.agent_first_logout is a valid timestamp in "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ" format
    And agent_log.total_login_time_hrs is a string representing a decimal number (e.g., "9.0")
    And agent_log.agent_city is "New York"
    And agent_log.agent_state is "NY"
    And agent_log.agent_country is "USA"
    And agent_log.agent_zip_code is "10001"
    And agent_log.data_loaded_at is a valid timestamp in "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ" format
    And agent_log.agent_key is a non-null string of 64 hexadecimal characters

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | unix_id | agent_name | log_date    | agent_first_login     | agent_first_logout    | total_login_time_hrs | data_loaded_at        | agent_key                                      |
      | H234              | IU007   | Dana Grey  | 2025-01-08  | 2025-01-08T08:00:00Z | 2025-01-08T17:00:00Z  | 9.0                  | 2025-01-08T18:01:00Z  | <SHA256 of all fields>                         |

  Scenario: Frequency and trigger validation
    Given the agent_log calculated field extraction job is scheduled
    When the scheduled time is reached
    Then the job runs and updates agent_log and agent_log_error_log as per the latest source data

  Scenario Outline: Location field override validation
    Given session_tracking_data contains region_city "<region_city>", region_state "<region_state>", region_country "<region_country>", postal_code "<postal_code>" for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log.agent_city is "New York"
    And agent_log.agent_state is "NY"
    And agent_log.agent_country is "USA"
    And agent_log.agent_zip_code is "10001"

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | region_city | region_state | region_country | postal_code |
      | I567              | Los Angeles | CA          | USA           | 90001       |
      | J890              | Miami       | FL          | USA           | 33101       |

  Scenario Outline: Data loaded timestamp validation
    Given the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs at "<run_time>"
    Then agent_log.data_loaded_at is set to "<run_time>"

    Examples:
      | run_time               |
      | 2025-01-09T18:01:00Z   |
      | 2025-01-10T18:01:00Z   |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - inconsistent data in joins
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>"
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with person_identifier "<person_identifier>", email_address "<email_address>"
    And agent_profile_data contains multiple records with email_address "<email_address>", last_modified_timestamp values that are identical
    When the agent_log calculated field extraction job runs
    Then agent_log_error_log contains a record with:
      | error_type    | "NonDeterministicMostRecent" |
      | error_message | "Multiple agent_profile_data records for email_address <email_address> have identical last_modified_timestamp" |
      | error_time    | "<data_loaded_at>"           |
    And agent_log does not contain a record for person_identifier "<person_identifier>"

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | email_address         | data_loaded_at        |
      | K123              | agent6@company.com    | 2025-01-11T18:01:00Z |

  Scenario: Indexing and partitioning validation
    Given agent_log table is updated with new records
    When the number of records exceeds 1 million
    Then agent_log table must be partitioned by log_date
    And agent_log table must have an index on agent_key

  Scenario: Performance validation
    Given agent_log calculated field extraction job runs on a dataset with more than 1 million records
    When the job completes
    Then the job duration must be less than 10 minutes

